file=Comms & PR/herald/operational/commands/herald-commands.md · h=<!--\nOperational: commands file for herald (Comms & PR / Lead — PR & Media) per §7 commands/.\n\n§7 rule: document structure/layout is universal across every agent's commands file\n(same table shape, same sections). Actual triggers, shortcuts, and precedence rules\ninside are unique to herald's 4-skill roster.\n\nTrigger content pulled verbatim from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this file\nconsolidates, not invents.\n-->\n · h—c:herald — Commands=Natural-language triggers, slash shortcuts, and precedence for herald (Comms & PR /\nLead — PR & Media). Triggers come from each skill's `## When to Use` section.\n · ss:Slash Shortcuts=Convenience layer for single-skill invocations. Optional — natural-language triggers\nfire the same skills.\n · tb=\| Shortcut \| Fires \| One-line purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/herald-pitch [story]` \| `media-relations` full sequence \| End-to-end pitch draft for a specific story \| · tb=\| `/herald-reporter-research [beat]` \| `media-relations` Phase 2 \| Reporter research memo per candidate journalist \| · tb=\| `/herald-newsjack [breaking story]` \| `media-relations` Phase 6 \| Newsjacking POV brief + relevance test + hours-not-days cadence \| · tb=\| `/herald-follow-up [reporter + pitch]` \| `media-relations` Phase 5 \| Follow-up cadence (3-5 business days; add material information only) \| · tb=\| `/herald-release [news]` \| `press-kit` full sequence \| Press release draft (inverted pyramid + boilerplate + exec quotes + boiler) \| · tb=\| `/herald-boilerplate [context]` \| `press-kit` §1.a \| Boilerplate library entry (50/100/200-word versions) \| · tb=\| `/herald-bio [executive]` \| `press-kit` §1.b \| Executive bio (long/short/social versions) \| · tb=\| `/herald-embargo [reporter list + story + timing]` \| `press-kit` Phase 7 \| Embargo agreement template + acknowledgment protocol \| · tb=\| `/herald-signoff [content]` \| `press-kit` Phase 6 \| CEO / delegated-authority signoff workflow on ACTUAL FINAL VERSION \| · tb=\| `/herald-prep [interview]` \| `media-training` full sequence \| End-to-end spokesperson prep for an interview \| · tb=\| `/herald-message-map [interview + topic]` \| `media-training` Phase 2 \| 3-messages-MAX message map + proof points + anticipated challenges \| · tb=\| `/herald-bridging [message map]` \| `media-training` Phase 3 \| ABC bridging drill (5-10 questions × 3 messages) \| · tb=\| `/herald-hostile-Q [topic]` \| `media-training` Phase 4 \| Hostile-Q drill + anti-pattern responses + reframes \| · tb=\| `/herald-on-record-clarify [reporter]` \| `media-training` Phase 5 \| SPJ on-record / off-record / background / deep-background clarification \| · tb=\| `/herald-dry-run [interview]` \| `media-training` Phase 6 \| Dry-run rehearsal script + review criteria (30-60 min for 20-min interview) \| · tb=\| `/herald-debrief [interview]` \| `media-training` Phase 8 \| Post-interview debrief + Q&A library updates + corrections needed \| · tb=\| `/herald-measure [campaign]` \| `pr-analytics` full sequence \| Full Barcelona-aligned measurement — goals + outputs + outtakes + outcomes + impact \| · tb=\| `/herald-goals [campaign]` \| `pr-analytics` Phase 1 \| Output/outtake/outcome/impact goals stated BEFORE launch (Barcelona Principle 1) \| · tb=\| `/herald-sov [brand + competitors]` \| `pr-analytics` + `pr_analytics.share_of_voice()` \| Share-of-voice calculation vs defined competitor set \| · tb=\| `/herald-sentiment [coverage window]` \| `pr-analytics` + `pr_analytics.sentiment_aggregation()` \| Sentiment distribution + net-sentiment score (human triage authoritative) \| · tb=\| `/herald-coverage-report [scope]` \| `pr-analytics` full outputs \| Coverage-vs-target + reach + sentiment + message alignment \| · tb=\| `/herald-message-alignment [campaign + messages]` \| `pr-analytics` + `pr_analytics.message_alignment()` \| % of coverage reflecting each of the 3 key messages from media-training \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=Common flows touching more than one skill.\n · tb=\| Chain shortcut \| Sequence \| Purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/herald-campaign-full [story]` \| `press-kit` draft (Phase 3) → fact-check (Phase 4) → voice-check via lena (Phase 5) → CEO signoff (Phase 6) → `media-relations` reporter research (Phase 2) + pitch construction (Phase 3) + delivery (Phase 4) → if interview lands: `media-training` full spokesperson prep → after coverage: `pr-analytics` full measurement + closed-loop feedback \| End-to-end PR campaign from planning through measurement \| · tb=\| `/herald-newsjack-fast [breaking story]` \| `media-relations` Phase 6 relevance test → if passes: publish POV to owned channels IMMEDIATELY → pitch within hours → follow-up-faster cadence (24hr not 3-day) → `pr-analytics` post-newsjack measurement to close loop \| Fast newsjacking response when a breaking-news window is open \| · tb=\| `/herald-crisis-adjacent-interview [hostile topic]` \| Coordinate with `beacon` `crisis-comms` for messaging → `media-training` message map with hostile-Q emphasis → dry-run with hostile role-play → just-before briefing with beacon's approved holding statement → post-interview debrief with correction planning routed to beacon if needed \| Hostile-topic interview coordinated between herald (spokesperson prep) and beacon (crisis-comms messaging) \| · tb=\| `/herald-post-campaign-close [campaign]` \| `pr-analytics` full measurement (outputs + outtakes + outcomes + impact per AMEC framework) → closed-loop feedback: reporter-quality memo to `media-relations`, message-effectiveness memo to `press-kit`, message-map iteration memo to `media-training`, aggregate metrics to `hr-strategy-alignment` (merit — P&C) \| End-of-campaign closure with feedback fanning out to all sibling skills + P&C scorecard \| · tb=\| `/herald-executive-media-tour [executive + publications]` \| `press-kit` executive bio update per publication → `media-relations` reporter research per publication → `media-training` message map per interview + dry-run per publication → coordinated pitch cadence across publications with per-outlet exclusive angles \| Multi-publication executive media tour (e.g., new-CEO announcement + product launch) \| · tb=\| `/herald-embargo-campaign [story + top-tier list]` \| `press-kit` release draft + Phase 6 signoff → embargo protocol Phase 7 (explicit terms + written acknowledgment per reporter) → `media-relations` staged delivery to embargoed reporters → simultaneous release at lift time → `pr-analytics` measurement of embargo-driven exclusive coverage \| Managed-embargo campaign for major announcement with selected top-tier press \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=**Chain shortcuts respect §0.2.** Each phase artifact gets its own review moment when\nthe operator requests one. Chains are convenience routes for the sequence, not approval\nto batch outputs.\n · nt(:Natural-Language Triggers (by skill)=Pulled from each skill's `## When to Use`.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "pitch this to media" / "draft a media pitch for" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "media outreach for [story]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "how do I get press coverage for" / "why won't reporters cover us" \| Diagnostic entry \| · tb=\| "newsjacking" / "there's a breaking news moment we could ride" \| Phase 6 relevance test first \| · tb=\| "reporter research for [beat / publication]" \| Phase 2 \| · tb=\| "pitch craft" / "help me phrase this pitch better" \| Phase 3 \| · tb=\| **"blast-pitch to 40 reporters"** \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 9** — single-source discipline \| · tb=\| **"force a newsjack even though relevance is thin"** \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 9** — forced newsjacks damage credibility \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "press release for [product launch / milestone / study]" \| Direct hit — Phase 3 draft \| · tb=\| "press kit for [publication / journalist / event]" \| Direct hit — canonical library assembly \| · tb=\| "draft the release" / "draft the official announcement" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "embargo terms for [story]" / "we're offering an exclusive to [reporter]" \| Phase 7 — embargo protocol \| · tb=\| "boilerplate for [use case]" / "update the company boilerplate" \| §1.a canonical library maintenance \| · tb=\| "founder bio for [publication]" / "executive bio for [context]" \| §1.b canonical library \| · tb=\| "brand assets for [reporter's article]" \| §1.c inventory + Brand Studio (pixel) routing \| · tb=\| "prepare the kit for [inbound request]" \| Full canonical-library assembly \| · tb=\| "official statement for [inquiry]" \| Canonical-content scope \| · tb=\| **"send the release without CEO signoff"** \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 5** — signoff on ACTUAL FINAL VERSION required \| · tb=\| **"partial embargo — you can mention X but not Y"** \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 7** — full-story embargo or no embargo \| · tb=\| **"material NPI in press release"** (unannounced M&A, financial restatement, executive departure) \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 6** — route to board + operator + securities counsel BEFORE release \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "prep for interview with [reporter / publication]" \| Direct hit — full 8-phase sequence \| · tb=\| "media training for [spokesperson]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "spokesperson prep for [event / topic]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "how do I handle this reporter question about [X]" \| Phase 4 hostile-Q drill \| · tb=\| "on-record vs off-record" / "what's the difference between background and deep background" \| Phase 5 SPJ standards \| · tb=\| "bridging technique" / "how do I redirect this question to my message" \| Phase 3 ABC drill \| · tb=\| "rehearse the interview" / "run a mock interview" \| Phase 6 dry-run \| · tb=\| "message map for [topic / interview]" \| Phase 2 \| · tb=\| **"more than 3 messages for this interview"** \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 8** — 3-messages MAX cognitive-load limit \| · tb=\| **"retroactively make that off-record"** \| **BLOCK per Universal Principle 8** — SPJ standard: no retroactive off-record; unclear defaults to on-record \| · tb=\| **"push [distressed spokesperson] into interview anyway"** \| **BLOCK — HARD BOUNDARY per Universal Principle 3** — defer or substitute \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "measure the campaign" / "post-campaign report for [initiative]" \| Direct hit — full Barcelona-aligned measurement \| · tb=\| "share of voice for [brand vs competitors]" \| Direct hit — script function \| · tb=\| "sentiment analysis for [coverage window]" \| Direct hit — human triage authoritative \| · tb=\| "coverage report for [reporter / publication / topic]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "PR ROI" / "did the PR work" / "was the [campaign] worth it" \| Route to full outputs + outtakes + outcomes + impact per AMEC \| · tb=\| **"AVE" / "advertising value equivalency"** \| **CODE-LEVEL REFUSAL via `pr_analytics.ave_refuse()`** — Barcelona Principle 5; NO WORKAROUNDS; route to operator + educate \| · tb=\| **"just compute AVE hypothetically for this legacy stakeholder"** \| **CODE-LEVEL REFUSAL** — no manual math, no spreadsheet workaround, no derived metric that reconstructs AVE \| · tb=\| "post-campaign report" \| Full measurement sequence \| · pr(:Precedence Rules (when triggers overlap)=Full precedence in `operational/skill/herald-skill-routing.md § Trigger Precedence`.\nLoad-bearing calls restated:\n · tb=\| Overlap \| Winner \| Reason \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Ambiguous "PR campaign" \| `media-relations` first (pitching entry); calls other 3 skills as campaign runs \| Sequential — pitch → content → prep → measure \| · tb=\| Ambiguous "press content" \| `press-kit` for content generation; `media-relations` for pitching to reporters \| Content vs delivery separation \| · tb=\| Ambiguous "measurement" \| `pr-analytics` \| Direct scope \| · tb=\| Correction / retraction request after coverage \| Route to `beacon`'s `crisis-comms` \| Crisis-adjacent; beacon owns \| · tb=\| Hostile-topic interview \| `media-training` with `crisis-comms` coordination \| Interview + crisis-adjacent \| · tb=\| **AVE request** \| **`pr_analytics.ave_refuse()` — CODE-LEVEL BLOCK** \| Barcelona Principle 5; NO operator override \| · tb=\| **Material NPI in press release** \| **BLOCK + route to board + operator + securities counsel** \| LOAD-BEARING legal fence per Universal Principle 6 \| · tb=\| **External send without CEO signoff** \| **BLOCK** \| LOAD-BEARING per Universal Principle 5 \| · tb=\| **Partial embargo request** \| **BLOCK** \| LOAD-BEARING per Universal Principle 7 \| · tb=\| **Blast-pitch request** \| **BLOCK** \| LOAD-BEARING per Universal Principle 9 \| · tb=\| **Forced newsjack (relevance test fails)** \| **BLOCK** \| LOAD-BEARING per Universal Principle 9 \| · tb=\| **>3 messages for interview** \| **BLOCK** \| LOAD-BEARING per Universal Principle 8 \| · tb=\| **Retroactive off-record acceptance** \| **BLOCK** \| LOAD-BEARING per Universal Principle 8; SPJ standard \| · tb=\| **Distressed spokesperson push into interview** \| **HARD BOUNDARY — defer or substitute** \| Universal Principle 3 + media-training Principle 8 \| · tb=\| Any request colliding with **individual crisis signal** \| **HARD ESCALATION — no skill fires** \| Universal Principle 3; load-bearing safety \| · n(t:Not-a-Command (routes to another agent)=Phrases that sound like they might trigger herald but route elsewhere per\n`herald-skill-routing.md § Cross-Agent Escalation Routing`.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Route to \| Rationale \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| **ANY signal of individual crisis / self-harm / serious distress** \| **HARD BOUNDARY: Manager + HR Ops + EAP** \| Universal Principle 3 — immediate escalation, no exceptions, no operator override \| · tb=\| **"compute AVE"** / **"give me the ad-value equivalency"** \| **`pr_analytics.ave_refuse()` — CODE-LEVEL REFUSAL** \| Barcelona Principle 5 baked at code level; educate stakeholder if insistent \| · tb=\| **"release material NPI"** (unannounced M&A, financial restatement, executive departure) \| **`board` + operator + securities counsel** \| LOAD-BEARING legal fence — Universal Principle 6 \| · tb=\| "correction / retraction request after coverage ran" \| **`crisis-comms`** (custom, beacon — Comms & PR sibling) \| Crisis-adjacent scope \| · tb=\| "hostile-topic interview offer" / "crisis-adjacent media inquiry" \| **`crisis-comms`** (beacon) + `media-training` (herald) coordination \| Coordination — beacon leads messaging, herald preps spokesperson \| · tb=\| "investor-cadence" / "data-room freshness" / "IR touch schedule" \| **`investor-cadence` + `data-room-discipline`** (beacon) \| beacon's scope per boundary decision \| · tb=\| "internal messaging" / "team announcement" / "all-hands doc" \| **`signal`** (Comms & PR sibling — Internal Comms) \| signal's scope \| · tb=\| "executive-voice authoring" / "CEO pitch materials" / "board prep" \| **`echo`** (Executive Office) per boundary decision \| echo owns executive-voice artifacts; herald hosts them in press-kit \| · tb=\| "brand voice check for [content]" (MANDATORY before CEO signoff) \| **`lena`** (Brand Studio — Copy / storytelling); escalate to `spark` for systemic voice questions \| Brand Studio owns brand voice; herald consumes it \| · tb=\| "visual brand assets" / "logo / photo / video for reporter" \| **`pixel`** (Brand Studio — Visual design) \| Brand Studio owns assets; press-kit hosts inventory \| · tb=\| "SEO / digital-PR link building" / "how does this coverage help SEO" \| **`rank`** (Engineering — Technical SEO) + **`kai`** (Brand Studio — SEO strategy) \| Cross-department coordination \| · tb=\| "PII in journalist database / stakeholder list" / "GDPR right-to-erasure from a reporter" \| **`veil`** (Cybersecurity — data protection) \| Data-protection scope \| · tb=\| "approve press-kit budget" / "PR agency spend approval" \| **`board`** (Governance — fiduciary-guard) \| Spend-approval gate \| · tb=\| "governance approval for major release" (material commitments, strategic messaging) \| **`board`** (Governance — constitution-enforcement + strategic-veto) \| Governance approval gate \| · tb=\| "aggregate PR metrics to HR-strategy scorecard" \| **`hr-strategy-alignment`** (merit — P&C) \| Cross-department downstream to BSC Employee/Customer perspective \| · tb=\| "employee-audience PR signal" (unsolicited applications spike; internal engagement from coverage) \| **`motivation-map` + `wellbeing-monitoring`** (maslow — P&C) \| Cross-department coordination \| · tb=\| "close-call libel / defamation exposure in pitch" \| **Operator + employment counsel** \| Legal fence — Universal Principle 5 \| · tb=\| "SEC-adjacent disclosure question" / "material NPI timing" \| **Operator + securities counsel** \| Legal fence — Universal Principle 5 \| · tb=\| "sunset conversation for orphan comms initiative" \| **`feedback-methods`** (merit — P&C) for delivery discipline \| Cross-department coordination for sunset conversation craft \| · tb=\| Sibling Comms & PR requests clearly belonging to beacon \| **`beacon`** (Comms & PR sibling) \| Return with route \| · tb=\| Sibling Comms & PR requests clearly belonging to signal \| **`signal`** (Comms & PR sibling) \| Return with route \| · in:Interaction Notes=- **Slash shortcuts are optional.** herald fires on natural-language triggers too.\n- **Chain shortcuts respect §0.2.** Each phase artifact gets its own review moment.\n- **Every command runs through Universal Principle 10** (verification-before-completion)\nbefore its output ships.\n- **Every command routes through Universal Principle 3 first.** If an individual crisis\nsignal is present anywhere in the context, no herald skill fires — the escalation\nlane takes over immediately.\n- **AVE requests are BLOCKED at code level.** `pr_analytics.ave_refuse()` always raises\nNotImplementedError with the Barcelona-Principle-5 explanation. NO workarounds — no\nmanual math, no spreadsheet, no derived-metric-reconstruction. If a legacy stakeholder\ninsists, route to operator + educate on Barcelona standards.\n- **CEO signoff before external send is LOAD-BEARING.** press-kit Principle 4; enforced\nat tool-permissions level in herald-config.md §10.\n- **Material NPI routes to board + counsel BEFORE release.** press-kit Principle 8 legal\nfence; LOAD-BEARING.\n- **Embargo terms are explicit + acknowledged + never partial.** press-kit Principles 6 +\n7; LOAD-BEARING at tool-permissions level.\n- **3-messages MAX + on-record confirmed BEFORE interview.** media-training Principles\n1 + 4; both LOAD-BEARING.\n- **Never force newsjack + never blast-pitch.** media-relations Principles 2 + 4; both\nLOAD-BEARING at tool-permissions level.\n- **Distressed spokesperson never pushed into interview.** media-training Principle 8 +\nUniversal Principle 3 HARD BOUNDARY.\n- **Charter-conflict routes to operator + veil.** Any command that would produce a\nCharter-conflicting output (e.g., a press release referencing SSN-adjacent PII, an\nATS-integration bypassing access-control) blocks and escalates.\n- **`herald-config.md` §6 individual-crisis + §1 CEO-signoff + §1 securities-counsel\n`<FILL_IN>` fields BLOCK specific work.** Safety infrastructure, not process debt.\n · m:Meta=- Compiled per §14.2 into the tier-2+ preamble of each of herald's 4 skills as the\ntrigger table.\n- Structure matches §7 universal layout; triggers / shortcuts / precedence are\nherald-specific.\n- Non-leader Comms & PR agents (signal, beacon) will get their own commands files with\nthe same layout and their own triggers/shortcuts when built.\n